    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="62e42fc8-80f3-5c16-9d00-a6bd8ab08200" activityNameId="ea0c60af-9bf5-5455-9f8c-633453420724" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Yeast paste, from whey, at fermentation</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Yeast paste, from whey, at fermentation
The multioutput-process "whey, to fermentation" delivers the co-products Ethanol, 95% in H20, from whey",  "yeast paste from whey", and "portein concentrate rom whey". The allocation is based on economic criteria. The production of ethanol from whey is of no economical importance in the world.;
UUID: 2e22fe81-a5ab-3ab9-80ea-e70d9a1c2f6f
Fermentation of whey including materials, energy uses, infrastructure, and emissions.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Production of ethanol from whey with the Carbery process.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: The world production of ethanol from whey was 6.8 Million litres per year.
Sampling: Literature data 
Extrapolations: Some data are derived from other or unknown plants or have been estimated.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_2e22fe81-a5ab-3ab9-80ea-e70d9a1c2f6f.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
